WEBVTT

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.350
What happened here?

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.760
Well, so long as it's clean...

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:44.950
Onii-chan?

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:49.350
What do you want for dinner tonight?

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.520
Let's see.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.100
I feel like beef.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.330
How would you feel about sukiyaki?

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:58.200
Sukiyaki. Got it.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.500
I'll do the cleaning.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.170
It's okay.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.930
I'm thinking of doing whatever
I can from now on.

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:11.110
I can't let you do everything
for me forever.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.740
Onii-chan, help!

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.740
Elis, turn it off!

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:32.900
Evergreen Innocence

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.470
I'm home.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:39.370
Welcome back.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.160
Elis, where's the meat?

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.180
Meat?

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.400
If we don't have meat, we
can't make sukiyaki.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.190
I'm sorry, I'll go back out and get it.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.980
I'll do it this time.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.230
Stay here and cook the rice.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.310
I'll go get it.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.340
It's fine.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.960
But I...

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:17.000
You were up early cleaning, doing the
laundry, and making breakfast.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.470
You don't have to do all of that.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.380
We can do things the
way we always have.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:24.780
Okay.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:26.270
Later.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.750
This is exhausting.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:59.260
Maybe I can't live with
Onii-chan any more.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.760
I'm full.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.760
My stomach hurts.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.470
Onii-chan, your phone.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:18.200
Incoming call

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:19.940
Hello?

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.770
Good to hear from you, Shoko Nee-chan.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.540
A babysitter?

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:30.500
Yeah. Shoko Nee-chan asked me to
look after her kid this weekend.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.310
Who's Shoko Nee-chan?

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.990
I think she's a cousin from my
dad's side of the family.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:45.550
I have to attend a friend's wedding, and my
husband's currently working overseas.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:49.930
Then I remembered you, Hiroki...

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:54.180
Haruna's a five year old
girl. Would you mind?

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.110
Of course not!

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.790
Maybe we could go to an amusement
park or aquarium.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.380
This'll be fun.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:00.860
Yeah.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:06.080
Having a kid along might be better than
spending time alone with Elis...

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:10.520
It might improve this uncomfortable
mood...

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:12.280
It could help...

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.310
Maybe...

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:17.630
Come in.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.070
Welcome.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.790
Excuse the intrusion.

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.500
Hello, Haruna-chan.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.310
Mom, where's my book?

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.970
It's in your backpack.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:32.200
I'll help you find it.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:33.910
I can do it.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.290
I'm sorry.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.780
She's been very shy these days.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:40.090
I see.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.700
Elis was like that once, too.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.370
She's been obsessed with
picture books lately.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.380
She reads them all day.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.670
It'll certainly be easier
to look after her...

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:52.830
if she'll just be quietly reading.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:54.570
Oh, here.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.300
This Zashiki Warashi is a local specialty.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.310
You like these, don't you?

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:01.930
I haven't had these in forever.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:03.790
Zashiki Warashi?

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:08.650
The box says there's 12, but
for some reason there's 13.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:20.770
Your parents were very interested
to know what you've been up to.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:22.530
I see.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:27.200
Parents worry about their children
no matter how old they get.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.240
To put it better, you're flexible.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.350
To put it worse, you're indecisive.

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:35.710
It's both a positive and negative quality.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:37.880
I see.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:41.810
Good thing you're quiet,
unlike your mom.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:44.650
You won't be saying that for long.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:45.680
Huh?

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:48.000
Look at the time!

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:52.180
I wish I could stay longer, but I've
got an appointment at the salon.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.390
I need to get going.

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:57.860
Haruna, listen to them
and be a good girl.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.550
Take good care of her.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.740
See you.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:14.380
I'm already exhausted.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:17.270
Haruna-chan, is that book interesting?

00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:19.870
I guess so.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.150
The weather's nice outside.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:25.200
Is there anywhere you'd like to go?

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:26.760
Huh?

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:30.060
Elis, let sleeping bears lie.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:32.090
No one's asleep.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:35.020
Just let her read her books.

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:38.070
But she came all the way here.

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:40.410
What is it, Haruna-chan?

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.770
Do you want some juice, Haruna?

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:48.710
There's a place I've always
wanted to visit.

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.920
Where? Where do you want to go?

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:53.620
The amusement park? The aquarium?
A department store?

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:57.350
Tell us, Haruna.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.460
Suttamonda Jump Fortress.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:03.730
What?

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:06.400
Suttamonda?

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.900
The Gandala series?

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:15.710
I'm Princess Gandala.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:19.240
I'm on a quest to free
my imprisoned soul.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:22.280
I know this book.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:27.220
It seems kind of familiar to me, too...

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:29.960
You read this to me when I was little.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.160
I did.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:35.300
I didn't realize this book
was still around.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.100
Buraman!

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.030
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:44.700
And Chao.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:45.640
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.470
Chao's a lot more beautiful, though.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:50.310
Sorry about that.

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:53.240
If we hurry, we can make
the evening ritual.

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:55.430
Evening ritual?

00:08:55.430 --> 00:09:00.280
In order to save her captured soul, we
have to learn all kinds of “Pakku”...

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:07.020
and reach Suttamonda Jump Fortress before
dusk to break the witch's spell.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:09.910
That's the evening ritual.

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:10.690
I see...

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:13.780
Buraman, Chao, hurry!

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:14.630
Okay!

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:16.590
Let's go, Onii-chan.

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:21.550
Where are we supposed to go?

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:33.120
Is this the eastern forest, Chao?

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:35.150
Yes, Princess Gandala.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:43.730
We have to steal the witch's spell.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:44.840
Her spell?

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:45.530
Yeah.

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:51.170
Quickly, go steal her spell.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:54.450
The witch...

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:55.640
I see.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:58.790
If she catches you, she'll
turn you into a frog...

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:00.080
so be careful.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:03.760
I don't know what to do about
my mischievous child.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.490
What are you talking about?

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:08.190
Your child listens to you.

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:10.450
I'm too old for this.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:14.010
What am I supposed to
say if they catch us?

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:18.610
I think we've already been
turned into frogs.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:19.470
Huh?

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:22.310
Are you playing tag?

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:23.880
What a good father.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:24.870
Father?

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.860
See you later, dad.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:28.120
Hey!

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:32.040
Kids these days...

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:36.250
We have learned the spell,
Princess Gandala.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:38.180
Good work.

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:42.620
Elis, I mean Chao, don't run away.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.130
We've got a long road ahead of us.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:47.070
We don't have time to mess
around, Buraman.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.560
Why are you getting into this?

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:53.000
Because it's fun.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:57.930
Next we'll collect the egg of
the golden bird of grief.

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:59.050
Okay.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:01.310
There's more?

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:05.980
The curse is broken once we've
overcome the seven trials.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:10.640
Could you narrow it down to three?

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:23.790
There it is.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:28.680
Gacha Gacha...

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:30.830
I need to get some change.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:41.910
I want a yellow egg.

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:46.620
It's Buraman's job to get the egg.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:49.300
Just 300 more yen, Haruna.

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:50.620
The yellow one.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:52.790
They all contain the same thing.

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:54.710
No!

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:59.080
I want the yellow one.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:00.900
They all contain the same thing.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:03.330
No!

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.470
What are you smiling about, Onii-chan?

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:11.910
Hooray!

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.700
The yellow egg!

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:18.080
That's great, Haruna... I mean,
Princess Gandala.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.380
Yeah.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.320
What's next?

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:26.390
Laugh at your reflection in the
blue water three times.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:28.060
Here you are.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:36.580
Blue water...

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.700
It looks delicious.

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:43.530
I see.

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.780
Isn't this good, Chao?

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.810
Yes, Princess Gandala.

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:52.020
Buraman, what are you drinking?

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:55.350
Huh? This is, uh...

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:59.780
A soup stewed from the roots of trees from
the headwaters of the Upside Down River...

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:01.760
that will grant him the fourth Pakku.

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:03.690
That.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:09.070
There are three Pakku remaining.

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:12.030
There's three more?

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:26.920
What did I do to deserve this?

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:30.770
You can do it, Buraman!

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:34.330
Karate chop the Southern Cross!

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:40.330
I'll karate chop the author of that book!

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:04.640
Princess Gandala, the
bridge is unsteady.

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:06.440
Watch your step.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:18.300
Once we cross this bridge,
the final trial will be...

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.110
Buraman?

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:24.640
Help me!

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:29.160
That didn't happen in the book.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:30.990
You look like an idiot, Buraman.

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:34.050
It's just a little extra...

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:37.170
You're heartless!

00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:42.190
We're supposed to climb this?

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:49.730
Suttamonda Jump Fortress
is at the top of this cliff.

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:51.990
Haruna-chan, you must be tired.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:54.040
Do you want to continue this tomorrow?

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:57.470
No! I'm going to the fortress!

00:14:57.610 --> 00:14:59.410
Okay, okay.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.900
Looks like Haruna-chan fell asleep.

00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:15.190
Yeah. Let's get to the top.

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:15.960
Okay.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:22.100
I used to carry you just like this.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.720
Really?

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:29.680
You'd tire yourself out following
me everywhere I went...

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:32.680
and end up asking me to carry you.

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:39.100
I've always played the
princess' bodyguard.

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:45.870
And I've always been
your younger sister.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:54.700
Princess.

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:56.470
Princess Gandala.

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:01.030
We've arrived at Suttamonda
Jump Fortress, Princess.

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:24.600
It's Suttamonda Jump Fortress.

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:27.500
Quickly, the spell to break
the witch's curse!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.600
Yes, Princess Gandala.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:40.580
Abudala Amidala Gandala, release
the princess' imprisoned spirit!

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:54.240
The curse of imprisonment
has been broken.

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:56.280
Chao, Buraman?

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.010
Yes.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:16:59.220
Kiss.

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:01.130
What?

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:04.610
You want us to kiss?

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:06.400
I do!

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:08.480
Kiss.

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:13.510
But that isn't in the book.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:16.130
It's Princess Gandala's command.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:21.000
If you kiss, the imprisoned soul
will awake from its slumber.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.620
What should we do, Onii-chan?

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:27.060
Let's just get this over
with and go home.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:29.860
Get this over with?

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:34.990
Princess, we shall do it.

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:35.800
Very good.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:39.670
Onii-chan?

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:44.170
One, two, and...

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:54.350
Three!

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:03.630
11, 12, 13...

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:06.860
14, 15, 16...

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:13.930
Tada!

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:17.040
Special Suttamonda Jump
Fortress fried rice!

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:19.480
Amazing!

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:21.550
Isn't it great, Haruna-chan?

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:22.510
Yeah.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:24.700
Haruna-chan, do you want milk?

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:25.650
Yeah.

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:29.250
Let's get you a bib.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:30.370
Okay.

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:37.360
Huh? Do you want milk too, Onii-chan?

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:42.030
No, I'm starving. Let's have dinner.

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:43.760
Let's eat!

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.470
Let's eat!

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:54.280
Haruna-chan's asleep.

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:55.330
Yeah.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:00.380
By the way, where are
you going to sleep?

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:06.090
I'm going to be sore tomorrow.

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:10.390
You did climb a lamppost.

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:12.070
Don't laugh at me.

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:16.370
I can't believe she'd make a scrawny
humanities student do that.

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:18.790
That took all my strength.

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:23.270
And you asked us to save
you in a crosswalk.

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:32.350
We'll wake Haruna.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:36.110
That was fun.

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:38.000
Yeah...

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:49.030
What beautiful weather!

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.700
Thank you.

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:59.410
I had a blast all the way to the
wedding's third after party.

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:01.850
Did you have trouble looking after her?

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:03.510
It was unbelievably...

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:04.960
It was fun.

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:09.980
Playing with Haruna-chan made
me feel like a kid again.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:12.220
You heard her.

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:14.770
I'm glad you enjoyed yourselves.

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:18.450
Say good bye, Haruna.

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:22.230
Buraman, Chao, good work.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:23.570
Take care.

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:24.900
Yes, ma'am.

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:27.240
Behave yourself.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.910
Thank you for everything.

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:31.840
Bye!

00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:33.700
Bye, Haruna-chan!

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:34.690
See you again!

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:36.010
Bye!

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.290
She's gone.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:47.120
Hey, Onii-chan?

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:52.960
Sorry for worrying you.

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:55.630
What's that for?

00:20:55.890 --> 00:20:59.010
I'm fine now.

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:01.160
I see.

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:10.810
Hey, uh...

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:13.750
I'm fine.

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:13.460
Sepia is the color of memories.

00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:17.090
The nostalgic color that captures
joy and sadness.

00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:18.320
Hey, Onii-chan...

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:20.610
What do you think of a girl with a past?

00:23:20.610 --> 00:23:22.170
The mystery could be interesting.

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:27.050
Something like, “I was betrayed
by a man and can't go on”...

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:32.020
or “I treat men like playthings
and throw them away?”

00:23:32.020 --> 00:23:33.490
Why does her past have to be so awful?

00:23:33.490 --> 00:23:36.020
Next episode, “Sepia Triangle.”

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:38.820
Those with a heavy past are
regarded with caution!
